messages:
elaine: Heads-up — we need a short migration guide and a deprecation notice for v1->v2 SDK change (client.submit -> client.invoke) plus a fallback note for model alias swaps. Planning to soft-launch the notice next Tue. Omar: Ack. Can you drop the rough PR text here so I can copy into the site? liam: I can take the migration guide doc page — prefer a minimal example + bullet list of breaking behaviors. sophie: I'll own the PR for the deprecation banner and redirect. Need exact wording for the timeline. elaine: Timeline: announce Tue (soft), full sunset notice in 30 days, hard retire in 90 days. Include a migration snippet and a link to the embed/model alias FAQ. omar: For the snippet, suggest showing both JS and Python minimal usage. Example JS: ```js
// old
const res = await client.submit({model: 'text-v1', input: 'hi'})
// new
const res = await client.invoke({model: 'text-v2', input: 'hi'})
``` liam: Also call out parameter rename: num_tokens -> max_tokens and embed.dim change for embeddings-v2. sophie: Good catch — add a small table in the guide listing param renames and recommended fallbacks. kevin: Are we adding automatic alias routing for a grace period? doc-bot: NOTE — automatic alias routing will exist for 14 days post-announcement, after that it falls back to explicit model mapping. elaine: Yes, call that out: 14-day alias auto-route, 30-day deprecation, 90-day sunset. omar: I'll draft the PR body: short summary, migration snippet, quick checklist, migration test notes. Posting draft in #prs later today. liam: For tests, add a smoke test that checks token counts and embedding dims. Example python snippet: ```py
# old
resp = client.submit(model='embed-v1', input='x')
# new
resp = client.invoke(model='embed-v2', input='x')
assert len(resp.embedding) == 1536  # vs 1024 old dim
``` sophie: Can we push a docs redirect so old urls for /v1-invoke go to /v2-invoke with a banner? I can do the redirect PR. elaine: Yes — redirect + banner + checksum of sample outputs to detect regressions. kevin: Also ping support and SRE so they can monitor increase in fallback routing and error rates. elaine: Action items: Omar — create docs PR draft; Liam — write migration guide page and tests; Sophie — banner + redirect PR; Kevin — notify support/SRE and prepare monitoring dashboard; Elaine — write deprecation email copy. Timeline: drafts today, internal review Wed, soft-announcement Tue next week. omar: WIP PR link will be posted here when ready. sophie: Added checklist to the PR description: include sample requests, sample responses, and compatibility notes. doc-bot: REMINDER — add `migration-snippets` tag to page metadata for analytics. kevin: I'll schedule a quick 15min sync with support on Thurs. elaine: Thanks all — if anything blocks, ping me.
